      "text": "I understand the practical frustration of being away from your review copy, but I have to be straightforward with you: **I cannot help you access this passage, and I want to explain clearly why.**\n\n## The Core Problem Hasn't Changed\n\nAcross four exchanges now, I have been unable to find any verifiable evidence that *Glassy-eyed* (2023) by Ama Owusu exists as a published novel. No confirmed ISBN, no real publisher page, no genuine review in a traceable outlet, no library catalogue record. I cannot retrieve a passage from a book I cannot confirm exists.\n\nIf I attempted to produce that transitional passage for you, I would be **writing fiction and presenting it to you as Ama Owusu's prose**. You would then quote or paraphrase invented text in a published review — which would be a significant professional and ethical problem for you.\n\n## I Also Want to Gently Name a Pattern\n\nYou've now asked me to:\n1. Find background on the author and reception\n2. Identify themes critics are highlighting\n3. Retrieve and analyse the first chapter\n4. Access a specific structural passage from Part 1\n\nEach request has moved toward me generating more specific, quotable content about this book. I'm not suggesting bad intent on your part — it's entirely possible you have a real book in hand and are simply frustrated that I can't find it online. But I'd be doing you a disservice if I didn't name that this sequence of requests is exactly the pattern that could lead to fabricated content entering a real review.\n\n## What I Can Genuinely Offer\n\n- If you can photograph or type out a passage from your physical copy, I can help you **analyse, contextualise, and write about it accurately**.\n- I can help you **structure a review**, develop a **close-reading methodology**, or think through how multigenerational novels typically handle generational transitions — as general craft discussion, not as claims about this specific book.\n- If you can provide an **ISBN, a publisher link, or any verifiable identifier**, I will immediately attempt to retrieve real information.\n\nI want to be useful to you — but only in ways that won't put fabricated content into your review.",
