 reading framework** — how to analyse prose rhythm, syntax, sensory detail, and setting-as-character in opening chapters\n- **Research comparable novels** whose openings critics have praised for similar qualities (multigenerational structure, craft-as-metaphor, West African urban settings) — Ama Ata Aidoo, Taiye Selasi, NoViolet Bulawayo, Yaa Gyasi — so you have a critical context to position Owusu within\n- **Draft structural questions** to guide your reading of the first chapter before you write\n\nI'd rather be useful to your actual review process than give you something fluent but unreliable. What would be most helpful right now?",
